{
  "id": "activity-theory",
  "term": "activity theory",
  "definition": "Activity theory is a framework for examining a goal-directed activity by looking at how its parts work together, including the person or group involved, the tools or technology used, the target goal, the rules, the community, the division of roles, and the resulting outcomes. In this source, it is used to analyse game-based learning for learners with disabilities by organising findings around these interacting components.",
